By adding this method to your class using the [PexMethod] attribute, you are making sure that Pex will generate a test for this method.

The [PexAssumeUnderTest] attribute allows you to ignore any side-effects from your test code, which should improve the speed and performance of your PEX tests.

The test will be run until it can generate an infinite number of tests. If there is any side-effect or branch condition based on a test condition, Pex will stop the generation as it cannot figure out a new test case based on the current status.

If Pex was unable to generate 1000 more tests, it will pause the test execution to ensure that the results of its exploration do not change inadvertently. By specifying a more comprehensive test or with more complex input data, you can improve the execution time to accommodate more exploration results.--------------------            if (New_Ret == false) 
